{"name":"Riviera Beach","hex":"#c0ae96","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Riviera Beach","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A city in Palm Beach County, Florida, United States.","A census-designated place in Anne Arundel County, Maryland, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Riviera_Beach"}],"entries":[{"title":"Riviera Beach, Florida","blocks":[{"text":"Riviera Beach is a city in Palm Beach County, Florida, United States, which was incorporated on September 29, 1922. Due to the location of its eastern boundary, it is also the easternmost municipality in the Miami metropolitan area. In the 2020 U.S. census, the total population of Riviera Beach residents was 37,604 people."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Welcome_to_Riviera_Beach_Florida_Sign_%2844179413804%29.jpg/330px-Welcome_to_Riviera_Beach_Florida_Sign_%2844179413804%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Riviera_Beach%2C_Florida"},{"title":"Riviera Beach, Maryland","blocks":[{"text":"Riviera Beach is a census-designated place in Anne Arundel County, Maryland, United States. The population was 12,677 at the 2010 U.S. census."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/2016-08-15_11_46_31_View_south_along_Maryland_State_Route_173_%28Fort_Smallwood_Road%29_just_south_of_Bar_Harbor_Road_in_Riviera_Beach%2C_Anne_Arundel_County%2C_Maryland.jpg/330px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Riviera_Beach%2C_Maryland"},{"title":"Riviera","blocks":[{"text":"Riviera is an Italian word which means 'coastline', ultimately derived from Latin rīpa, through Ligurian rivêa. It came to be applied as a proper name to the coast of Liguria in the form Riviera ligure, then shortened in English."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/English_Riviera.jpg/330px-English_Riviera.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Riviera"},{"title":"Beach","blocks":[{"text":"A beach is a landform alongside a body of water which consists of loose particles. The particles composing a beach are typically made from rock, such as sand, gravel, shingle, pebbles, etc., or biological sources, such as mollusc shells or coralline algae. Sediments settle in different densities and structures, depending on the local wave action and weather, creating different textures, colors and gradients or layers of material."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Beach_at_Fort_Lauderdale.jpg/330px-Beach_at_Fort_Lauderdale.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beach"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/1d/Seal_of_Riviera_Beach%2C_Florida.png/120px-Seal_of_Riviera_Beach%2C_Florida.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/1d/Seal_of_Riviera_Beach%2C_Florida.png/250px-Seal_of_Riviera_Beach%2C_Florida.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/1d/Seal_of_Riviera_Beach%2C_Florida.png/120px-Seal_of_Riviera_Beach%2C_Florida.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASeal_of_Riviera_Beach%2C_Florida.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Riviera_Beach_Maryland_segregation.png/250px-Riviera_Beach_Maryland_segregation.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2a/Riviera_Beach_Maryland_segregation.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_conte